<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- Store Network cockpit: trade-area median household income (x) vs store
     lifetime sales (y), one point per store, no basemap - a straight JR7
     xy scatter (dataset kind="xy"), single series, legend off per the brief.
     Every store's postal_fsa resolves to a fsa_demographics row (330 of 330,
     0 orphans on the join - verified 2026-08-25), so this is a plain INNER
     JOIN with no NULLIF/COALESCE guarding needed.

     Field types: storenumber Integer (established convention across this
     suite, e.g. net_map.jrxml); total_sales is a persisted DECIMAL(14,2)
     column on stores selected with no arithmetic, so BigDecimal; median_income
     on fsa_demographics is itself unadorned integer arithmetic
     (46000 + inc_h * 1000, no DECIMAL cast) in build_fsa_demographics.sql, so
     it is declared java.lang.Long here rather than Integer - a JDBC getLong()
     widens cleanly off either an INT4 or INT8 physical column, so Long is the
     safe superset regardless of which one the CTAS actually produced, and
     matches the convention this suite already uses for other unadorned
     integer-arithmetic results (chn_kpi.jrxml's scored_customers).

     DEVIATION from the task brief's literal chartType="xyScatter": the local
     compile rejected it outright - InvalidFormatException naming
     ChartTypeEnum's real values, which include SCATTER (name "scatter") but
     no xyScatter/xyScatter-shaped constant at all (the only "xy"-prefixed
     entries are XYAREA/XYBAR/XYLINE, none of which is a plain point scatter).
     chartType="scatter" is JasperReports' actual keyword for the same
     dataset kind="xy" point-per-row chart the brief describes. The brief's
     capital-V xValueExpression/yValueExpression also turned out wrong for
     the SAME reason net_map.jrxml's xyz series needed lower-case v:
     JRDesignXySeries's real properties, per the UnrecognizedPropertyException
     naming all six, are xvalueExpression/yvalueExpression/labelExpression/
     autoSort/itemHyperlink/seriesExpression - lower-case v on BOTH the xy and
     xyz series classes in this JR 7.0.6 build, not just xyz. Corrected here
     to match.

     RENDER GOTCHA, found on the first run-to-PDF: chartType="scatter" reuses
     the SAME underlying plot class as the line chart family, so a bare plot
     element with no line/shape flags rendered every one of the 330 points
     connected by a jagged teal line in x-sort order (a "connect the dots"
     mess, not a scatter read) - the JR7-native form's plot class is fixed by
     chartType per jr7-valid-elements.md, and for scatter that class turned
     out to be the JRLinePlot family, not a dedicated point-only plot. Added
     showLines="false" showShapes="true" (the same two flags
     jr7-valid-elements.md documents for a linePlot/JRLinePlot) to get
     unconnected point markers only, matching the brief's "each point is one
     store" intent.

     Single series, chart in the title band -> evaluationTime="Report".
     Cockpit archetype: no parameters. -->
<jasperReport name="net_income_scatter" pageWidth="720" pageHeight="320" columnWidth="700" leftMargin="10" rightMargin="10" topMargin="10" bottomMargin="10">

	<query language="SQL"><![CDATA[
SELECT f.median_income, s.total_sales, s.storenumber
FROM stores s
JOIN fsa_demographics f ON f.fsa = s.postal_fsa
	]]></query>

	<field name="median_income" class="java.lang.Long"/>
	<field name="total_sales" class="java.math.BigDecimal"/>
	<field name="storenumber" class="java.lang.Integer"/>

	<title height="300">
		<element kind="image" x="0" y="0" width="36" height="36" scaleImage="RetainShape" hImageAlign="Left" vImageAlign="Top"><expression><![CDATA["repo:/images/actian_logo"]]></expression></element>
		<element kind="staticText" x="0" y="0" width="700" height="20" fontSize="14.0" bold="true" forecolor="#1F4E79" hTextAlign="Center"><text><![CDATA[Trade-Area Income vs Store Sales]]></text></element>
		<element kind="staticText" x="0" y="22" width="700" height="14" fontSize="9.0" forecolor="#5B7DA6" hTextAlign="Center"><text><![CDATA[Each point is one store]]></text></element>

		<element kind="chart" chartType="scatter" x="0" y="40" width="700" height="256" showLegend="false" evaluationTime="Report">
			<dataset kind="xy">
				<series>
					<seriesExpression><![CDATA["Stores"]]></seriesExpression>
					<xvalueExpression><![CDATA[$F{median_income}]]></xvalueExpression>
					<yvalueExpression><![CDATA[$F{total_sales}]]></yvalueExpression>
				</series>
			</dataset>
			<plot showLines="false" showShapes="true">
				<seriesColor order="0" color="#1DB6C0"/>
			</plot>
		</element>
	</title>

</jasperReport>
